rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · From test flights to aerial scouting"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/the-legacy-of-ingenuity-the-frontier-of-extraterrestrial-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · The legacy of Ingenuity"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/resource/ingenuity-mars-helicopter-by-the-numbers/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity by the numbers"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"]]]]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"16",". ","Scientific and technological legacy"],["P",{},"The first question was whether a small helicopter could fly on Mars at all. You followed the air, the energy and the decisions that made the answer possible. Ingenuity went on to offer another view of the ground: one that could help a rover team decide where to look and how to get there. The experiment had become useful in ways a short first hop could only suggest. The final flight left damaged blades and an incomplete view of the landing. Engineers built the best explanation the evidence allowed, and kept the uncertainty visible. That is part of the work, too. Ingenuity will not take off again. The next aircraft can still learn from every flight it made."],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","Scientific and technological legacy",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_f_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_f_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P",{"role":"status"},"Stopped"]],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Scientific sources"],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.go