he flight."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Read a status report in its time"],["P",{},"The January 19 report described what was known immediately afterward. It was not yet the completed accident investigation. Later evidence and analysis changed what engineers could reasonably explain."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","A report written just after an event and a later investigation answer different questions."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/flight-72-status-update/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Flight 72 status, January 19, 2024"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/ingenuity-helicopter-flight-log.pdf","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Completed flight log (PDF)"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","A short hop to check the aircraft",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_13_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_13_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P",{"role":"status"},"Stopped"]]],["DETAILS",{"data-archive-record":"damage-evidence"},["SUMMARY",{},"What the pictures established"," — ","Reference access; not yet discovered"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"After Flight 72 · observed damage"],["P",{},"Communications were reestablished the following day. Later imagery showed rotor-blade damage that ended Ingenuity’s ability to fly. The images establish damage; they do not provide a complete eyewitness view of touchdown."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"Keep observation separate from explanation"],["P",{},"An image of a damaged blade is direct evidence of its condition. Describing the exact motions and loads that produced it requires a reconstruction using the available flight data and engineering analysis."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","The 3D model remains an intact engineering visualization. It is not a reconstruction of the damaged aircraft after Flight 72."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/after-three-years-on-mars-nasas-ingenuity-helicopter-mission-ends/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · End of flight mission, January 25, 2024"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","What the pictures established",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_14_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_14_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P",{"role":"status"},"Stopped"]]],["DETAILS",{"data-archive-record":"likely-scenario"},["SUMMARY",{},"A most-likely explanation"," — ","Reference access; not yet discovered"],["P",{"class":"record-context"},"December 11, 2024 · later accident-investigation account"],["P",{},"NASA’s investigation linked too few trackable surface features to unreliable motion estimates. Its most-likely scenario involved excessive horizontal motion, a hard impact on a sand-ripple slope, rapid changes in attitude and damaging rotor loads."],["SECTION",{},["H4",{},"The limit of the evidence"],["P",{},"Engineers considered multiple viable scenarios. The available data supported a most-likely account, not certainty about every motion. Testing navigation over a broader range of terrain and improving robustness are sensible lessons from this case."]],["P",{"class":"record-relevance"},["STRONG",{},"Why it matters:"]," ","State which parts are observed and which are inferred. An honest uncertainty statement is part of a good engineering explanation."],["UL",{"class":"evidence-sources"},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/missions/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-helicopter/nasa-performs-first-aircraft-accident-investigation-on-another-world/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Accident investigation, December 11, 2024"," ",["SPAN",{"class":"sr-only"},"(opens in a new tab)"]]]],["DETAILS",{"class":"listen-mode"},["SUMMARY",{},["svg",{"aria-hidden":"true","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","width":"22","height":"22"},["path",{"d":"M4 15V9a8 8 0 0116 0v6l-3 5H7zM7 8h10v7H7z","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"1.5"}]]," Helmet Listen Mode"],["P",{},"Listen to ","A most-likely explanation",". Original text stays available. Browser voices vary; word-by-word synchronization is not provided."],["P",{},"Audio is muted. ",["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Unmute audio"]],["DIV",{"class":"listen-controls"},["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Listen / Replay"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button","disabled":""},"Pause narration"],["BUTTON",{"type":"button"},"Stop narration"]],["LABEL",{"for":"_r_15_"},"Narration speed"],["SELECT",{"id":"_r_15_"},["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"0.75"},"0.75","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"true","value":"1"},"1","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.25"},"1.25","×"],["OPTION",{"__playwright_selected_":"false","value":"1.5"},"1.5","×"]],["LABEL",{},"Voice volume",["INPUT",{"__playwright_value_":"1","aria-label":"Voice volume","min":"0","max":"1","step":"0.1","type":"range","value":"1"}]],["P",{"role":"status"},"Stopped"]]],["H2",{},"Historical timeline"],["BUTTON",{},"2020-07-30",": ","Launch with the Mars 2020 mission."],["BUTTON",{},"2021-02-18",": ","Arrival at Jezero Crater beneath Perseverance."],["BUTTON",{},"2021-04-03",": ","Deployment onto the Martian surface."],["BUTTON",{},"2021-04-04",": ","First independent night survived."],["BUTTON",{},"2021-04-19",": ","First powered, controlled flight on another planet."],["BUTTON",{},"2021-05-07",": ","Fifth flight completes the initial demonstration series."],["BUTTON",{},"2023-04-13",": ","Fiftieth flight."],["BUTTON",{},"2024-01-18",": ","Flight 72: the final flight."],["BUTTON",{},"2024-01-25",": ","NASA announces the end of the flight mission."],["BUTTON",{},"2024-12-11",": ","NASA describes the accident investigation’s most-likely scenario."],["DETAILS",{},["SUMMARY",{},"Scientific sources"],["UL",{},["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/mission/mars-2020-perseverance/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Ingenuity mission and timeline"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/3d-resources/ingenuity-mars-helicopter/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/Brian E. Kumanchik · Ingenuity 3D model"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/mars_2020/ingenuity/landing/mission/spacecraft/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Spacecraft engineering"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.jpl.nasa.gov/news/press_kits/ingenuity/landing/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA/JPL · Original demonstration objectives"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/news-release/nasas-ingenuity-mars-helicopter-succeeds-in-historic-first-flight/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · Historic first flight, April 19, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://science.nasa.gov/blog/its-cold-on-mars/","target":"_blank","rel":"noopener noreferrer"},"NASA · It’s Cold on Mars, April 2, 2021"]],["LI",{},["A",{"href":"https://www.nasa.gov/solar-system/nasas-mars-helicopter-survive